; claude: the picture the Image* examples take apart, in its three
; formats (made by make_demo_pictures.py), embedded as strings:
; Demo_pictures.demo_picture_png, _gif, _jpg (see
; scripts/build/files_to_string_ml.ml), which software/ and web/
; copy_files like the examples' sources
(rule
 (targets Demo_pictures.ml)
 (deps demo_picture.png demo_picture.gif demo_picture.jpg %{project_root}/scripts/build/files_to_string_ml.ml)
 (action
  (with-stdout-to
   %{targets}
   (run ocaml %{project_root}/scripts/build/files_to_string_ml.ml demo_picture.png demo_picture.gif
     demo_picture.jpg))))

; claude: five 3D examples aren't in this list, only in software/ (and
; the web ones): Cube3d, InteractiveCube3d, PaintersAlgorithmFail3d,
; FloatingCity3d, Corridor3d. The OpenGL backend's own
; "m"/"b"/"f"/"i"/"o" debug keys (see README.md) don't include
; PaintersAlgorithmFail3d's "z" or Corridor3d's "c" (plan_opengl.md
; scoped painter's-algorithm out, since a hardware z-buffer makes the
; toggle moot); InteractiveCube3d needs a HUD. None of that explains
; Cube3d or FloatingCity3d, which render fine on every other backend
; (including WebGL, see plan_webgl.md) -- they're just not wired into
; this executable list yet.
